[{:db/id "q-104134/selection/532ea50f6a360920be2e46da2c156b783e23d2c5d119c8d508b5bb30b9cc2f9d" :answer/id #uuid "bb72e652-2763-5ceb-bd0f-6c7a5e466cfa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104134/selection/5772b9b3900d18bb5761b1b2af447855baa36661dd869252c5abfe44c9ca1a12" :answer/id #uuid "8653a3ef-39f9-51eb-82b1-62da85d47edd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104134/selection/c5b95ad7f44e67a83e287a5432a787d2a86b38e3743a8fd0b5ba96f8da318c55" :answer/id #uuid "1e68694e-64b0-5d69-84a4-34468affad76" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 2 & -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104134/selection/6cbfe3c6b127ccd70b6daba31095cfb57284a06cdf91b3f09fd85d8a82a20bc7" :answer/id #uuid "c1212344-18db-586d-8738-9b91209147ed" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ -4 & -2 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104134/selection/5f9eea0dcea29bae9d7ac608b84fe9399d94775c2f42b268bc0d0d115e8a9b99" :answer/id #uuid "8e8799de-21d7-5edd-9209-467cd8efb73a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104134/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "3becfc88-cffb-5601-98b6-f559acc656b5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-104134/selection/6cbfe3c6b127ccd70b6daba31095cfb57284a06cdf91b3f09fd85d8a82a20bc7" :answer-field/choices ["q-104134/selection/532ea50f6a360920be2e46da2c156b783e23d2c5d119c8d508b5bb30b9cc2f9d" "q-104134/selection/5772b9b3900d18bb5761b1b2af447855baa36661dd869252c5abfe44c9ca1a12" "q-104134/selection/c5b95ad7f44e67a83e287a5432a787d2a86b38e3743a8fd0b5ba96f8da318c55" "q-104134/selection/6cbfe3c6b127ccd70b6daba31095cfb57284a06cdf91b3f09fd85d8a82a20bc7" "q-104134/selection/5f9eea0dcea29bae9d7ac608b84fe9399d94775c2f42b268bc0d0d115e8a9b99"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-104134" :question/id #uuid "fb4bf485-78fa-5095-a727-46d78e9ce455" :question/math-academy-id "q-104134" :question/problem "Find the inverse of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]$\ngiven that $det(A)=-1.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's follow the standard five-step procedure.\n\n**Step 1:** We are given the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A)=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2:** Form the matrix of the minors of $A.$\nTo make this matrix, we replace each entry of $A$ by its minor.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Create the matrix of cofactors by changing the sign of some of the entries of $M$ according to the rule of alternating signs.\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n**Step 4:** Write down the transpose of the matrix of cofactors.\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 2 & -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n**Step 5:** Use the formula for the inverse of a $3\\times 3$ matrix.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(-1)}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 2 & -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ -4 & -2 & 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-104134/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "50c01507-99a7-5328-8d74-c9e9bda51330"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-104134"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-73485/selection/6659a5e691490b233f65b21a623ba1e2d2741ff00091613c7da6936cdd94d7ff" :answer/id #uuid "1278584e-88c5-55fd-81cf-179b62403056" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{12}[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ -12 & 0 & -6\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73485/selection/f09d4c42a8d8dad6f51057cca415b38930aa10685c3814ac6f9a9a1c1fdd6b46" :answer/id #uuid "36dfbf46-be46-5e70-9b7a-6bdd6273122e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{12}[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & -12 \\\\ -1 & 4 & 18 \\\\ 3 & 0 & -6\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73485/selection/0507e4c95ec072cc7336cc16f7ad6a6942a46175506f45f040084d9915bf24fd" :answer/id #uuid "148a36ce-70ef-5668-b6e8-fbf694e2600e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{12}[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 18 \\\\ -12 & 0 & -6\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73485/selection/4932a0ed846fff0baff9dbf3f40be13b11ca6ea797a2f330e996dcc8c6a8aa09" :answer/id #uuid "8dad0546-0c0f-5836-afb9-77ece8d4330d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 12 \\\\ 1 & -4 & -18 \\\\ -3 & 0 & 6\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73485/selection/dcb275b7f0c1e497b19b4d4e4d3b9220461871592e5f114136e42d7d31284c12" :answer/id #uuid "57f646ce-3f7b-5385-92b2-c15f53f31c60" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 4 & 18 \\\\ 3 & 0 & -6\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73485/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "c9cb691e-d16b-5700-a5ff-50fa4e7c6dcd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-73485/selection/f09d4c42a8d8dad6f51057cca415b38930aa10685c3814ac6f9a9a1c1fdd6b46" :answer-field/choices ["q-73485/selection/6659a5e691490b233f65b21a623ba1e2d2741ff00091613c7da6936cdd94d7ff" "q-73485/selection/f09d4c42a8d8dad6f51057cca415b38930aa10685c3814ac6f9a9a1c1fdd6b46" "q-73485/selection/0507e4c95ec072cc7336cc16f7ad6a6942a46175506f45f040084d9915bf24fd" "q-73485/selection/4932a0ed846fff0baff9dbf3f40be13b11ca6ea797a2f330e996dcc8c6a8aa09" "q-73485/selection/dcb275b7f0c1e497b19b4d4e4d3b9220461871592e5f114136e42d7d31284c12"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-73485" :question/id #uuid "2d1042ad-eb6e-59f8-9dab-abab5265f662" :question/math-academy-id "q-73485" :question/problem "Find the inverse of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]$\ngiven that $det(A)=12.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's follow the standard five-step procedure.\n\n**Step 1:** We are given the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A)=12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2:** Form the matrix of the minors of $A.$\nTo make this matrix, we replace each entry of $A$ by its minor.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ -12 & -18 & -6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Create the matrix of cofactors by changing the sign of some of the entries of $M$ according to the rule of alternating signs.\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ -12 & 18 & -6\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n**Step 4:** Write down the transpose of the matrix of cofactors.\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & -12 \\\\ -1 & 4 & 18 \\\\ 3 & 0 & -6\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n**Step 5:** Use the formula for the inverse of a $3\\times 3$ matrix.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & -12 \\\\ -1 & 4 & 18 \\\\ 3 & 0 & -6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-73485/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "50c01507-99a7-5328-8d74-c9e9bda51330"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-73485"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-9967/selection/f139853a2532cf7864300fbe4e6f13e65fc4defa62355b3a55a7c39600edcb4e" :answer/id #uuid "139ba8ce-9b61-5c85-9a04-3655e842306b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -5 & 4 \\\\ 5 & -6 & 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-9967/selection/68425b7826fcece43ebf5f2ffdc829ef29c8675ef9395f3c5eae71dab7e41ce5" :answer/id #uuid "cc801eb8-0369-523b-a994-ebe95105fed9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -5 & 4 \\\\ 5 & -6 & 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-9967/selection/1f42caeff8ee33b969b2a36e0e42624cc343f010465eee6d91d659bc067628cb" :answer/id #uuid "51453a18-f217-50a1-bb63-13490f799f36" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -10 & -4 \\\\ 5 & -6 & 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-9967/selection/27935b27c10616b1c97c54bd6dee592f5340df53fe9754ac8d1acaa055139a16" :answer/id #uuid "11bd6433-215e-544c-a4e8-df83e70cad38" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -5 & -4 \\\\ 9 & -6 & 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-9967/selection/32db89a67881f397127c0eefb6a71d80e5ec6ca862c07e88e477ffb71a10bc90" :answer/id #uuid "c0ff5db1-40da-5f98-a90c-e50ddf7ff9cd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -10 & 4 \\\\ 5 & -6 & 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-9967/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "ffd42d47-a772-50ff-89e8-99a1278df0dd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-9967/selection/f139853a2532cf7864300fbe4e6f13e65fc4defa62355b3a55a7c39600edcb4e" :answer-field/choices ["q-9967/selection/f139853a2532cf7864300fbe4e6f13e65fc4defa62355b3a55a7c39600edcb4e" "q-9967/selection/68425b7826fcece43ebf5f2ffdc829ef29c8675ef9395f3c5eae71dab7e41ce5" "q-9967/selection/1f42caeff8ee33b969b2a36e0e42624cc343f010465eee6d91d659bc067628cb" "q-9967/selection/27935b27c10616b1c97c54bd6dee592f5340df53fe9754ac8d1acaa055139a16" "q-9967/selection/32db89a67881f397127c0eefb6a71d80e5ec6ca862c07e88e477ffb71a10bc90"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-9967" :question/id #uuid "c8e0bc68-4b39-55ac-8170-1361143f9b8e" :question/math-academy-id "q-9967" :question/problem "Find the inverse of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 8 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 7 & -2 & 4\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Let's follow the standard five-step procedure.\n\n**Step 1:** Find the determinant of $A.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A)=|\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 8 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 7 & -2 & 4\\end{aligned}| & =4|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 5 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{aligned}|-(-2)|\\begin{aligned}8 & 5 \\\\ 7 & 4\\end{aligned}|+3|\\begin{aligned}8 & -3 \\\\ 7 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =4(-12+10)+2(32-35)+3(-16+21) \\\\  & =-8-6+15 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2:** Form the matrix of the minors of $A.$\nTo make this matrix, we replace each entry of $A$ by its minor.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 5 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}8 & 5 \\\\ 7 & 4\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}8 & -3 \\\\ 7 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ 7 & 4\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 \\\\ 7 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 5\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ 8 & 5\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 \\\\ 8 & -3\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -3 & 5 \\\\ -2 & -5 & 6 \\\\ -1 & -4 & 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Create the matrix of cofactors by changing the sign of some of the entries of $M$ according to the rule of alternating signs.\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 2 & -5 & -6 \\\\ -1 & 4 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n**Step 4:** Write down the transpose of the matrix of cofactors.\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -5 & 4 \\\\ 5 & -6 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n**Step 5:** Use the formula for the inverse of a $3\\times 3$ matrix.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1}[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -5 & 4 \\\\ 5 & -6 & 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-9967/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "50c01507-99a7-5328-8d74-c9e9bda51330"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-9967"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-319395/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "d4cd7880-cbeb-5e17-a522-cdef933ac288" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-319395/field-1/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "d1569719-0ed3-55b5