122a778-d775-58c3-a04a-f92b984b0b10" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-319395/field-4" :answer-field/id #uuid "f655b395-ec65-58be-aad8-7318e72596a9" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-319395/field-4/10293ac0295e0e79554137a949f5c5c46b9812dcc0a3ecb6349c4cb5e6acdff3" :answer-field/choices ["q-319395/field-4/10293ac0295e0e79554137a949f5c5c46b9812dcc0a3ecb6349c4cb5e6acdff3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-319395" :question/id #uuid "29d21586-1288-572a-99e4-232cb8821d62" :question/math-academy-id "q-319395" :question/problem "Find the inverse of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -3 & -2\\end{aligned}].$\n\n|  |  | $-1$ | $-3$ | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${A}^{-1}=\\,\\,$ {{field-2}} |  | $-1$ | $3$ | {{field-3}} |  |\n|  |  | $0$ | {{field-4}} | $3$ |  |" :question/worked-solution "Let's follow the standard five-step procedure.\n\n**Step 1:** Find the determinant of $A.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A)=|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -3 & -2\\end{aligned}| & =(-3)|\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ -3 & -2\\end{aligned}|-0|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}|+1|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-3)(2-3)-0(\\,-2-(-3)\\,)+(-3+3) \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2:** Form the matrix of the minors of $A.$\nTo make this matrix, we replace each entry of $A$ by its minor.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ -3 & -2\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -3\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -3 & -2\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -3\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 3 & 9 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Create the matrix of cofactors by changing the sign of some of the entries of $M$ according to the rule of alternating signs.\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 3 & -9 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n**Step 4:** Write down the transpose of the matrix of cofactors.\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -9 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n**Step 5:** Use the formula for the inverse of a $3\\times 3$ matrix.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -9 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -9 & 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-319395/field-1" "q-319395/field-2" "q-319395/field-3" "q-319395/field-4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "50c01507-99a7-5328-8d74-c9e9bda51330"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-319395"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-319370/field-1/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" :answer/id #uuid "22354b23-f75c-50c2-80df-844f85a7f423" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-319370/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "11d42a07-0606-5394-ac28-4d1a35d2a48b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-319370/field-1/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" :answer-field/choices ["q-319370/field-1/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-319370/field-2/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "e301e6b9-3976-597e-9fb0-a8b45765d11c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-319370/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "bba4f7bc-587a-51c8-87e6-378d764722ad" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-319370/field-2/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer-field/choices ["q-319370/field-2/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-319370/field-3/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53" :answer/id #uuid "2fcc61cd-f851-511c-84a7-6d09f7a65d94" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-319370/field-3" :answer-field/id #uuid "2226d888-1340-59d6-8cbb-eeab11e30423" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-319370/field-3/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53" :answer-field/choices ["q-319370/field-3/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-319370" :question/id #uuid "9e3fe030-755d-5041-98d0-9545fc141827" :question/math-academy-id "q-319370" :question/problem "Find the inverse of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 3 & -2\\end{aligned}]$\ngiven that $det(A)=-4.$\n\n|  |  | $-1$ | {{field-1}} | $1$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${A}^{-1}=-\\frac{1}{4}\\,\\,$ |  | $4$ | {{field-2}} | $0$ |  |\n|  |  | $7$ | {{field-3}} | $1$ |  |" :question/worked-solution "Let's follow the standard five-step procedure.\n\n**Step 1:** We are given the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A)=-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2:** Form the matrix of the minors of $A.$\nTo make this matrix, we replace each entry of $A$ by its minor.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -2\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -2\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -4 & 7 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -9 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Create the matrix of cofactors by changing the sign of some of the entries of $M$ according to the rule of alternating signs.\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 4 & 7 \\\\ -3 & 4 & 9 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n**Step 4:** Write down the transpose of the matrix of cofactors.\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 7 & 9 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n**Step 5:** Use the formula for the inverse of a $3\\times 3$ matrix.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 7 & 9 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-319370/field-1" "q-319370/field-2" "q-319370/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "50c01507-99a7-5328-8d74-c9e9bda51330"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-319370"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-18288/selection/8ec14357d3854c200c63ee6d95b7d70d7b5a01610abf7cfcb767533bd16cfedb" :answer/id #uuid "24c35886-1555-5e0e-9203-46617d69f802" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{13}{71}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-18288/selection/46f5852bd9ee906d79fae20e39d87507cca0b1d7acb5cfcf97d311c9d690f954" :answer/id #uuid "07a0bca4-9872-5634-9895-3b35e4ee320b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{71}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-18288/selection/11979b37e4c741574f04eb4e8e172a9668d6c119ef0321fdb79ba592e0850622" :answer/id #uuid "e546d6d3-0978-54ea-bd1c-8e77c8bb8a0c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{13}{71}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-18288/selection/e6f56725f27c985f8ec557f1ce6e48e6d5c1b5c6fcf0ea94297cc831571b020c" :answer/id #uuid "4363b492-ca9e-5130-8408-aa4e22cda897" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{71}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-18288/selection/485ff480de974793ded40a4428c67645d40f3016474ba38cc7a2e46237c89bc0" :answer/id #uuid "d90bf246-234f-5eae-a0e2-7b9c68114c9e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{10}{71}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-18288/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "20c66934-93ee-5f6a-b0a2-d1d2c4a23fe1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-18288/selection/11979b37e4c741574f04eb4e8e172a9668d6c119ef0321fdb79ba592e0850622" :answer-field/choices ["q-18288/selection/8ec14357d3854c200c63ee6d95b7d70d7b5a01610abf7cfcb767533bd16cfedb" "q-18288/selection/46f5852bd9ee906d79fae20e39d87507cca0b1d7acb5cfcf97d311c9d690f954" "q-18288/selection/11979b37e4c741574f04eb4e8e172a9668d6c119ef0321fdb79ba592e0850622" "q-18288/selection/e6f56725f27c985f8ec557f1ce6e48e6d5c1b5c6fcf0ea94297cc831571b020c" "q-18288/selection/485ff480de974793ded40a4428c67645d40f3016474ba38cc7a2e46237c89bc0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-18288" :question/id #uuid "1c50173d-87e8-5fa9-94f9-84896e240170" :question/math-academy-id "q-18288" :question/problem "Determine the entry ${a}_{21}^{′}$ in the inverse of a matrix $A$ $=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 5 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 5 & -6 & 3\\end{aligned}]$ if its determinant is $71.$" :question/worked-solution "Since we want the entry ${a}_{21}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{12}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{12} & =(-1)^{1+2}|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 5 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 5 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-(-3-10) \\\\  & =13.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{21}^{′}=\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{12}=\\frac{1}{71}\\cdot 13=\\frac{13}{71}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-18288/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c704e019-035f-5807-b02d-62b9cd44c1c7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-18288"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-319416/field-1/6bb6fe4cbf49be857221580cc496029e4813795bce6a4086557bb8bc8141d0b9" :answer/id #uuid "d227f88a-1d1b-5106-92c1-bfd6998feac2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{13}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-319416/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "1808c969-ad9d-51b2-9fb1-aa521f99ebb0" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-319416/field-1/6bb6fe4cbf49be857221580cc496029e4813795bce6a4086557bb8bc8141d0b9" :answer-field/choices ["q-319416/field-1/6bb6fe4cbf49be857221580cc496029e4813795bce6a4086557bb8bc8141d0b9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-319416" :question/id #uuid "67ba84de-9203-5dc9-b081-a5adbd6f7175" :question/math-academy-id "q-319416" :question/problem "Determine the entry ${a}_{33}^{′}$ in the inverse of a matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 2\\end{aligned}].$\n\n${a}_{33}^{′}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(A)=|\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 2\\end{aligned}| & =1|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}|-(-2)|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}|+0|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1(2-(-3))+2(4-0)+0(6-0) \\\\  & =13.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{33}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{33}^{t}={c}_{33}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{33} & =(-1)^{3+3}|\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =+|\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(1+4) \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{33}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{33}^{t} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{33} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{13}\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{13}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-319416/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c704e019-035f-5807-b02d-62b9cd44c1c7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-319416"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-18286/selection/dfffee7e1ab8cf225e55276a36d959f366e09fcf98ab63e32039b560a763c7de" :answer/id #uuid "b004a483-509e-5f7e-b850-49deaa40ba76" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{39}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-18286/selection/fe408bb8584d9549e0a0c9ef3adf534b4545b6ad8bd71384d7efac8421910872" :answer/id #uuid "9e389c25-4fd3-5d66-8445-d944f69b0c43" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{13}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-18286/selection/5d203d81be6b1f21c7cbe6d18ae590d051bfddb9a061032d8830f1fd1ba116c5" :answer/id #uuid "9b83cfcb-0128-5d79-b6ef-3aec88ec01eb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{11}{39}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-18286/selection/3b526d0871203a7fa20c2a891525c650a26e23eb2a93fea36737a1cf4d4423af" :answer/id #uuid "cb6372fb-f32f-5978-bd94-a3e204be63a4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{13}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-18286/selection/372e4652316f3e45a79a9ae72981448d38c2fccb2e0e6559bc2bfc4296255b71" :answer/id #uuid "fc2eaecb-9e0a-54c5-a61e-66dfe5bfa99e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{39}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-18286/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "56e011d3-385d-567e-8459-e7e986ccbfdd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-18286/selection/372e4652316f3e45a79a9ae72981448d38c2fccb2e0e6559bc2bfc4296255b71" :answer-field/choices ["q-18286/selection/dfffee7e1ab8cf225e55276a36d959f366e09fcf98ab63e32039b560a763c7de" "q-18286/selection/fe408bb8584d9549e0a0c9ef3adf534b4545b6ad8bd71384d7efac8421910872" "q-18286/selection/5d203d81be6b1f21c7cbe6d18ae590d051bfddb9a061032d8830f1fd1ba116c5" "q-18286/selection/3b526d0871203a7fa20c2a891525c650a26e23eb2a93fea36737a1cf4d4423af" "q-18286/selection/372e4652316f3e45a79a9ae72981448d38c2fccb2e0e6559bc2bfc4296255b71"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-18286" :question/id #uuid "99ca9db9-93d5-5a9d-9021-745df58ebdc9" :question/math-academy-id "q-18286" :question/problem "Determine the entry ${a}_{32}^{′}$ in the inverse of the matrix $A$ $=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -1 \\\\ -3 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 3\\end{aligned}]$ if its determinant is $39.$" :question/worked-solution "Since we want the entry ${a}_{32}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{23}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{23} & =(-1)^{2+3}|\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-(-1-0) \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{32}^{′}=\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{23}=\\frac{1}{39}\\cdot 1=\\frac{1}{39}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-18286/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c704e019-035f-5807-b02d-62b9cd